Recycling diverts 35% of the US municipal waste stream from landfill — without it, the US would need to open new landfill capacity equivalent to the state of Rhode Island every decade.
Landfills are the third largest source of methane emissions in the US, a greenhouse gas 80× more potent than CO₂ over 20 years — reducing waste to landfill is a direct climate intervention.
In Germany, where recycling and composting rates exceed 65%, landfill use fell by 80% between 1990 and 2020 — demonstrating that high diversion rates are achievable at national scale.
